reatest showman what was  the stunt you asked she decided she  would convince the world that she gave  birth to a litter of rabbits in order to  do this  she put animal parts will say under her  skirt and acted out the process of  giving birth I guess in her mind she'd  be making enough money off this stunt to  eat rabbit meat every day for the rest  of her life doctors from around Europe  and visited and left fully believing in  her strange power even the king and  Prince of Wales bought it finally she  was caught sneaking rabbits into her  room and the jig was up but news of this  miracle had already spread far and wide  and her stunt resulted in people  thinking of rabbits as magical animals  people began banning rabbits do and  other harmful treatments allowing the  population to grow now that we covered  that let's move on to how top hats got  involved in all of this when top hats  started becoming popular in the late  1770s magicians picked up on its unique  shape and size allowing objects to be  easily concealed inside they started  borrowing them for shows in the rest is  history  although Louis compt was the first to  attempt the rabbit out of the hat trick  in 1814 it was John Henry Anderson that  made the trick what it is today his  marketing skills came in handy as he  created wooden posters of himself  producing rabbits from hats which drew a  worldwide attention  ever since then more and more magicians  have charted and the rabbit out of a hat  trick has truly become the face of magic  modern-day magicians definitely care  about their little hoppers no one ever  pulls rabbits by their ears that's a  common misconception magicians today  pickup the bunnies like any pet owner  would magicians are still careful to  keep their bunny sidekicks safe so safe  in fact that I even decided to trust in  the process and visit Fantasma magic  where I taught my pet bunny Leah to  disappear you want me to do a little  magic with Leah yes we can definitely  teach us some tricks bye Leah bye-bye  bye-bye I think  uh sorry we are sorry  Fantasma Magican yay  seriously uh awesome what a amazing  beautiful ribbon you use yes yes  as fun as learning magic was I think  it's safe to say Leo is happy to be back  in my arms we'll leave the magic to the  professionals  [Music]

